# Deploy to Production (FTP)

When the user asks to deploy, push, or upload files to the server, use the project deploy script.

## Command

From project root:

```bash
./scripts/deploy.sh <relative-path> [more-paths...]
```

Examples:

```bash
./scripts/deploy.sh wp-content/plugins/immobilgolf-helper/elementors/property.php
./scripts/deploy.sh wp-content/plugins/immobilgolf-helper/
```

Dry run:

```bash
./scripts/deploy.sh --dry-run wp-content/plugins/immobilgolf-helper/
```

## Rules

- Always deploy only the files or folders that were changed unless the user asks for a full sync.
- Paths must be relative to the project root.
- Credentials live in `deploy.env` (gitignored). Do not commit passwords.
- Do not deploy `wp-content/uploads`, cache folders, logs, or backup folders.
- After editing plugin files under `wp-content/plugins/immobilgolf-helper/`, offer to deploy those paths when the user wants changes on production.
